{%- comment -%}
  App embed — toggle this on once under Theme Editor → App embeds and it
  shows a "Book now" button site-wide with zero per-page setup, the same
  pattern other booking apps (e.g. Apntly) use for this. Trade-off vs.
  "GetBooqin Button" (the app block): you don't control exactly where it sits
  on the page, it always floats — in exchange, there's nothing to add to
  the theme per template.

  Unlike an app block, an app embed only gets Liquid's *global* scope — no
  `product` object is available here, per Shopify's own theme-app-extension
  docs — so this can't check page type or read product.handle in Liquid at
  all. booking.js already handles that: it parses the handle out of the
  current URL (/products/<handle>) instead, the exact fallback path it has
  for this case. Renders nothing except on an actual product page whose
  product is linked to a service.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'getbooqin.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'booking.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

<div class="getbooqin-product-embed getbooqin-product-embed--floating" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}></div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "GetBooqin",
  "target": "body"
}
{% endschema %}
